  "progression": "EER B2.5 minor requires 90 EC, of which at least 52 from year one, and no more than 8 outstanding concurrent EC for Amsterdam. Free and external minors need prior approval under B2.7. Research Skills starts after all year-one credits plus 26 from semester three and 20 from semester four. The supervisor must pass the proposal before the 12 EC BSc Assignment can start. The project is individual, with a scientific article and presentation. B4 assessment rules and the Amsterdam-specific table apply. The Amsterdam table does not add the separately credited Enschede societal-embedding unit. Continuous assessments carry credits within the displayed semester totals. Workshop safety under B1.2 and the first-year study-advice framework under A6.2 are separate conditions, not additional EC.",
